From 030e39011622b81cf8559b7e3174d0e85869e4eb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: XiangBo Kong <yarshure@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 12:37:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] nuageinit: mount the config drive read-only

The NoCloud / config-2 volume is only ever read, but rc.d/nuageinit
mounts it read-write.  When the hypervisor exposes that disk read-only
(Apple Virtualization.framework with a read-only disk attachment, QEMU
with readonly=on, ...) mount_msdosfs(8) fails with "Read-only file
system", the failure is ignored, and nuageinit later reports

  nuageinit: error parsing nocloud meta-data:
      /media/nuageinit/meta-data: No such file or directory

so no users, keys or hostname are configured.  Linux cloud-init mounts
the seed read-only as well.

Mount it with -o ro, and fail with a clear message if the mount fails.

Signed-off-by: XiangBo Kong <yarshure@gmail.com>
---
 libexec/rc/rc.d/nuageinit | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libexec/rc/rc.d/nuageinit b/libexec/rc/rc.d/nuageinit
index 43476a71c9eb..2210b15de6b6 100755
--- a/libexec/rc/rc.d/nuageinit
+++ b/libexec/rc/rc.d/nuageinit
@@ -49,7 +49,8 @@ nuageinit_start()
 	if [ -n "$drive" ]; then
 		mkdir -p /media/nuageinit
 		fs=$(fstyp $drive 2> /dev/null)
-		mount -t $fs $drive /media/nuageinit
+		mount -t $fs -o ro $drive /media/nuageinit || \
+		    err 1 "Unable to mount $drive"
 	else
 		product=$(kenv smbios.system.product)
 		case "$product" in
-- 
